  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759833,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 16 Years of Silence: A Commodore 64 Chronicle\n\n**16 Years of Silence** plunges you into the oppressive aftermath of Oceania’s victory, sixteen years after Winston and Julia’s rebellion. The Party’s grip has tightened, and any whisper of dissent is swiftly crushed. You play as Elias, a young archivist tasked with meticulously cataloging historical records – a seemingly innocuous role that masks a dangerous secret: he’s inherited fragments of Winston’s forbidden journal.\n\nGameplay blends exploration, puzzle-solving, and tense stealth sequences. Navigate the decaying, surveillance-laden streets of London, avoiding the ever-watchful eyes of the Thought Police. Decipher coded messages within the journal fragments to unlock memories and uncover a hidden resistance movement struggling to rekindle hope. \n\nThe game features a haunting soundtrack, evocative pixel art depicting a bleak and desolate future, and a branching narrative influenced by your choices. Can you piece together the truth, evade detection, and reignite the flame of rebellion, or will you become another casualty of the Party’s relentless control?  Your silence may be your only protection, but it also condemns you."
    },
